1. VNC: Virtual Network Computing

Examples
RealVNC
TightVNC

VNC uses the RFB protocol (Remote Framebuffer Protocol).
The server captures screen pixels
Sends framebuffer updates to client
Client sends back keyboard and mouse events

VNC does not automatically bypass NAT.
So to access the internet
	Port forward 5900 on router
	SSH tunneling

Default Port: TCP 5900

2. RDP: Remote Desktop Protocol
Native Windows protocol.
RDP protocol (Microsoft proprietary)

Default Port: TCP 3389
How It Works Internally

It sends drawing commands and not raw pixels
More bandwidth efficient.
Supports device redirection like printers, drives, clipboard.


3. TeamViewer

it does not require port forwarding
Uses cloud relay servers
Both devices connect outbound to TeamViewer servers
NAT traversal handled automatically

Ports used are 
Outbound: TCP 5938 (primary)
Fallback: 443 or 80

Both systems register with TeamViewer servers.
They exchange IDs.
Server establishes encrypted tunnel.
Either direct peer-to-peer or relay server.

4.  AnyDesk:

It is similar architecture to TeamViewer
Uses proprietary DeskRT codec
Efficient compression
Uses relay servers
NAT traversal automatic

Default outbound ports: TCP 80, 443, 6568
